  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "2a23196f-2aa1-403c-87fd-1d945849e102",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Vitamin D deficiency can cause a range of symptoms, from mild to severe. Here are some common symptoms of vitamin D deficiency:\n",
      "\n",
      "**Mild Symptoms:**\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Fatigue and weakness: Feeling tired, sluggish, and lacking energy.\n",
      "2. Muscle pain and cramps: Pain, cramping, and weakness in the muscles, especially in the legs, back, and arms.\n",
      "3. Joint pain and stiffness: Pain and stiffness in the joints, especially in the knees, hips, and back.\n",
      "4. Mood changes: Irritability, anxiety, and depression.\n",
      "5. Sleep disturbances: Difficulty sleeping, insomnia, or excessive sleepiness.\n",
      "6. Hair loss: Thinning or falling hair, especially in women.\n",
      "7. Skin problems: Acne, dermatitis, and other skin conditions.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Moderate Symptoms:**\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Bone pain: Pain in the bones, especially in the back, hips, and legs.\n",
      "2. Osteoporosis: Weakening of the bones, which can lead to osteoporosis and increased risk of fractures.\n",
      "3. Increased risk of infections: Vitamin D deficiency can weaken the immune system, making you more susceptible to infections.\n",
      "4. Digestive problems: Constipation, diarrhea, and other digestive issues.\n",
      "5. Weight gain: Unexplained weight gain, especially in the midsection of the body.\n",
      "6. Cardiovascular problems: High blood pressure, heart disease, and stroke.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Severe Symptoms:**\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Rickets: Softening of the bones in children, which can lead to bowed legs, stunted growth, and other skeletal deformities.\n",
      "2. Osteomalacia: Softening of the bones in adults, which can lead to bone pain, muscle weakness, and increased risk of fractures.\n",
      "3. Increased risk of autoimmune diseases: Vitamin D deficiency has been linked to an increased risk of autoimmune diseases, such as multiple sclerosis, type 1 diabetes, and rheumatoid arthritis.\n",
      "4. Cognitive impairment: Vitamin D deficiency has been linked to cognitive impairment, dementia, and Alzheimer's disease.\n",
      "5. Increased risk of certain cancers: Vitamin D deficiency has been linked to an increased risk of certain cancers, such as colon, breast, and prostate cancer.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Other Symptoms:**\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Seasonal affective disorder (SAD): Vitamin D deficiency has been linked to SAD, a type of depression that occurs during the winter months.\n",
      "2. Pregnancy complications: Vitamin D deficiency during pregnancy has been linked to an increased risk of preeclampsia, gestational diabetes, and other pregnancy complications.\n",
      "3. Neurological problems: Vitamin D deficiency has been linked to neurological problems, such as multiple sclerosis, Parkinson's disease, and epilepsy.\n",
      "\n",
      "It's essential to note that some people may not experience any symptoms of vitamin D deficiency, even if their levels are low. If you're concerned about your vitamin D levels, consult with your healthcare provider about getting tested and taking steps to maintain adequate vitamin D levels.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "llm = ChatGroq(\n",
